<section class="ags-wrap ags-faq"><div class="ags-faq-intro"><span class="ags-kicker">KNOW BEFORE YOU UPLOAD</span><h2>Good files.<br>Fewer surprises.</h2><p>Check the measured size before checkout. The file you upload is the complete sheet you are ordering.</p><a class="ags-text-link" href="/pages/file-guide">Read the file guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="ags-faq-list">
  <details><summary>Will you arrange my logos?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Upload the finished gang sheet you prepared. The app measures and prices it; artwork is not nested, combined, or rearranged.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What does quantity mean?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Complete copies of the uploaded sheet. Three copies means the entire file is printed three times, not three logos rearranged onto a new sheet.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Why 22-inch variants and a 22.5-inch limit?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>The variant name describes the commercial sheet size. This demo explicitly configures a 22.5-inch printable press limit. Your file still has to fit that limit.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What if my file is too large?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Genuine width overflow is rejected with the measured width and configured limit. Files longer than every variant are rejected. Measured-price files over 240 inches are rejected, not split.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Which file should I use?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A finished PNG with the intended page size and embedded resolution is a good starting point. The Studio and variant uploaders list their supported formats; the detailed PNG view accepts PNG only. Always review measured dimensions, especially when DPI metadata is missing.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Does this demo fulfill an order?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. This is an app-review environment with illustrative prices and test checkout. Nothing is physically printed or shipped, and no durability or turnaround guarantee is made.</p></details>
</div></section>
